A couple of problems have been spotted with xtb.

1) xtbd fails (exits) on HP-UX with the error "Alarm clock", (reported by
ronald@iti.gov.sg and aruba!glenr@uu2.psi.com)

The fix is to add a line to re-set the signal handler in the signal
handler code.

Add this line, in the function doalarm() in xtbd.c so that the last
four lines (lines 553-557) are:

        moveplayers();
        sendplayers();
        signal(SIGALRM,doalarm);        /* ADD THIS LINE */
        myualarm(100000);       /* reset 1/10th sec alarm */
        
2) xtb (and rtb) fail on machines with hostnames >15 chars (spotted by
jacob@cs.washington.edu)

This was caused by  my mis-reading of the gethostname(2) manual page,
which truncates the hostname, but *does not* null terminate returned
hostname if it was more than HOSTLEN.

A fix for this is to change:
        gethostname(sdata.extra.signon.hostname,HOSTLEN);
for:
        gethostname(sdata.extra.signon.hostname,HOSTLEN-1);
        sdata.extra.signon.hostname[HOSTLEN-1]='\0';

at line 518 in rtb.c and line 1277 in xtb.c.


I hope you enjoy the game.

